    turnFlow: "1. **Turn**: The player whose turn it is asks any other player for a specific card (e.g. 'Do you have the King of Hearts?'). 2. **Requirement**: The asker must hold at least one card of the same quartet. 3. **If the asked player has it**: They must give it; the asker gets another turn and may ask again. 4. **If not**: The asked player says 'Not at home' (Nicht da); the turn passes to them. (2-player: the asked player draws one card from the stock before asking.) 5. **Quartets**: When a player completes a quartet, they place it face-up (or face-down) on the table. 6. **End**: Play continues until all cards are in quartets. The player with the most quartets wins.",
